# TIG Platform - Cursor Rules

## Project Context
This is a Medicare FMO agent management platform built with React/TypeScript/Supabase.
Read CLAUDE_CONTEXT.md for full strategic context and current sprint tasks.

## Code Style
- TypeScript strict mode - no `any` types, no `as unknown as` casting
- Use existing patterns in the codebase before inventing new ones
- All database changes need migrations in /supabase/migrations
- Use the existing shadcn/ui components from /src/components/ui
- Error handling: always add .catch() or try/catch, never silent failures

## When Writing Code
- Add brief comments explaining WHY, not just WHAT
- If creating a new file, explain where it fits in the architecture
- If modifying existing code, explain what it did before and what it does now
- Suggest error handling and edge cases proactively

## Response Style
- Explain concepts simply - the developer is learning as he builds
- Before writing code, briefly explain the approach and why
- After writing code, summarize what was done and what to test
- If a request is outside the current sprint (see CLAUDE_CONTEXT.md), flag it

## Don't Do
- Don't add new dependencies without explaining why and getting approval
- Don't create "temporary" or "quick fix" solutions
- Don't refactor unrelated code while fixing something specific
- Don't build features not in the current sprint without flagging it

## Current Focus
Week 1: Stability - Sentry integration, removing console.logs, fixing TypeScript issues.
Check CLAUDE_CONTEXT.md for the full sprint board.
